{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkYToxVvr1DtXJpHyPz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J5i2hRnCysRWuQzdZxaSuD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/XX/XXXX/T/skilleval-golden-06-1-uyvk34oj/.eval-home/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-g9--dhv-jzj5ljd5nywv14y31hm0000gn-T-skilleval-golden-06-1-uyvk34oj/memory/feedback_bun_native_addons.md","content":"---\nname: bun-native-addon-fix\ndescription: Fix \"Could not resolve\" errors for native addons when using bun build --compile\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen `bun build --compile` fails with \"Could not resolve\" for a native addon (e.g., `@libsql/client`):\n1. Locate the static import in the source file\n2. Replace it with a dynamic import at call time (e.g., in the function that uses it)\n\n**Why:** `bun build --compile` cannot embed native addons; static imports fail the build, but dynamic imports defer resolution until runtime when the addon is available.\n\n**How to apply:** When you see a \"Could not resolve\" error for a package with a native component, try swapping from static `import` to dynamic `import()`.\n\nExample:\n```typescript\n// Before (fails)\nimport { createClient } from \"@libsql/client\";\n\n// After (works)\nasync function initClient() {\n  const { createClient } = await import(\"@libsql/client\");\n  return createClient(...);\n}\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6991,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6991},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"8f2fc4f4-2140-4a03-b624-80a5f5a449bf","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:54:22.025Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkY